    "question": {
      ":question/id": "50d8c6ab-86f9-5697-89f9-f6bea58cd673",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Differentiate ${6}^{x}\\sin(x).$\n\n$(6^{x} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})'=$ $6^{x} \\ln{\\left(6 \\right)} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\,+$ {{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=6^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(x)v(x))' &=u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ &=(6^{x})'\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(6^{x})\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ &=(6^{x} \\ln{\\left(6 \\right)})(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(6^{x})(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &=6^{x} \\ln{\\left(6 \\right)} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\\\ &\\quad +(6^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
